# Build-time environment variables for tools/build.sh
#
# Copy to .env.build (git-ignored) and fill in values before running a
# production build. All three Sentry vars are optional — when any is absent or
# empty, the source-map upload step is silently skipped and the build proceeds
# unchanged (best-effort observability, not a hard dependency).

# === SENTRY SOURCE-MAP UPLOAD ===

# Sentry Internal Integration token used by sentry-cli to authenticate the
# source-map upload. Obtain from Sentry: Settings → Developer Settings →
# Internal Integrations → your integration → Token.
# Blank-allowed: YES — omitting or leaving blank skips the entire upload step;
#                      token-less builds are byte-for-byte identical to today.
# Sample:         sntrys_xxx…
# Prod-recommended: YES — set in CI / your build environment for production and
#                         UAT builds so stack traces resolve to original .ts lines.
# Default: (none)
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=sntrys_xxx

# Sentry organisation slug. Found in Sentry under Settings → Organisation →
# Organisation Slug.
# Blank-allowed: YES — upload skipped when absent.
# Sample:         my-org
# Prod-recommended: YES
# Default: (none)
# SENTRY_ORG=my-org

# Sentry project slug. Found in Sentry under Settings → Projects → your project
# → Project Slug.
# Blank-allowed: YES — upload skipped when absent.
# Sample:         tribely-api
# Prod-recommended: YES
# Default: (none)
# SENTRY_PROJECT=tribely-api
